# Orca Fluke Edge-On Side Profile

In SharkVisuals OrcaBody, IMG_2273 side-profile flukes are horizontal so they appear as a short thin aft sliver (~2 units tall, ~1/4 body length) joining a slender peduncle. Do NOT draw a fat leaf (~8u tall, body-length). Flap with rotate-only about the peduncle hinge — no large y translation. Tighten orca viewBox left pad to match the short tip.

## Verification
- Verified: npm run lint && npm run build passed after rewriting OrcaBody caudal from fat leaf to ~2u edge-on blade; removed y-translate flap; tightened viewBox from -30 to 6
- Failure pattern avoided: Drawing orca flukes as a thick leaf/paddle (top-down width) in side view, then animating with y+rotate so they look wrong vs IMG_2273
- Dead-end ruled out: Keeping a long fat leaf caudal and only tweaking tip/notch — still reads as paddle, not edge-on horizontal flukes
